{"links":[{"id":"01069999f479","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":11,"p":[21,21],"r":[5,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. v. 1, LXX."},{"id":"bcfde8de64c5","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":19,"p":[94,94],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. ix. 9. 10."},{"id":"4afb60571b90","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":38,"p":[31,31],"r":[5,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. v. 7, 8."},{"id":"4d8120906aeb","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":66,"p":[22,22],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. ix. 9."},{"id":"bb2cf57bde42","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_mt","w":"chrysostomus.hom_mt","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":82,"p":[21,21],"r":[13,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"See Zech. xiii. 7. [The words \"of the flock\" are omitted, as in Mark xiv. 27. They do not occur in the passage in Zechariah.-R.]"},{"id":"d24b82eec31d","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":26,"p":[14,14],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. ix. 9"},{"id":"435b68349ba8","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":42,"p":[27,27],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. ix. 9"},{"id":"1db22d29744e","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":66,"p":[2,2],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. ix. 9"},{"id":"93df465e7e0b","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_jo","w":"chrysostomus.hom_jo","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":85,"p":[19,19],"r":[12,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xii. 10"},{"id":"15b3f194fe56","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":12,"p":[6,6],"r":[5,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. v. 2"},{"id":"887d27bb48a1","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":32,"p":[18,18],"r":[4,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"κορυφαιον, not of the Apostles, but of the Saints in general. The manner in which St. Paul is coupled with St. Peter, is remarkable, as in the Roman Breviary, Vesp. et Laud. Common. Cam. de Apost. \"Peter the Apostle, and Paul the Teacher of the Gentiles, these taught us Thy Law, O Lord. R. Thou shalt make them princes over all the earth.\" In the York Breviary, F. SS. App. Petr. et Paul, ad Vest. Hymn, St. 2. \"These are the two olive trees before the Lord (Zech iv. 3), and the candlesticks beaming with light, the two bright luminaries of Heaven.\" And again, non impar Paulus huic. St. Augustin observes, ad Bonif. cont. du. Ep. Pelag. 1, 3, c. 3, Ben. t. 10. \"When one says, `The Apostle, 0' without saying what Apostle, no one understands any but Paul, because he is best known from the number of his Epistles, and because he labored most.\" St. Maximus, Hom. 5, de Nat. Petr. et Paul, \"Therefore the blessed Peter and Paul are eminent among all, and have a kind of peculiar precedency, but between themselves, which is to be preferred to the other, is uncertain. For I think they are equal in merits because they are equal in suffering.\" He also says in the same Homily, \"To Peter, as to a good Steward, He gave the key of the Kingdom of Heaven. On Paul, as on an able Teacher, He enjoined the mastership in the teaching of the Church; that is, that whom the one has instructed unto salvation, the other may receive into rest; that whose hearts Paul hath opened by the teaching of his words, to their souls Peter may open the Kingdom of Heaven. For Paul too did also in a manner receive the key of knowledge from Christ.\" And St. Gregory, 1, 1 Dial. c. 12. \"The Apostle Paul is brother in Apostolical preeminence ( principatu ) to Peter, the first of the Apostles.\" See also St. Chrys. on Gal. i. 18, p. 25 O. T. where he says, \"equal in dignity with him, for at present I will say no more,\" and Gal. ii. 8, p. 34 O. T.; Tertull. adv. Marcion. 1, 5, and others. consider him especially intended in Jacob's blessing of Benjamin. St. Cyr. Hier. Cat. vi. p. 68, O. T. speaks of \"That goodly pair, Peter and Paul, the Rulers of the Church.\" Many more passages might be cited, but these may suffice to show in what esteem St. Paul was held among the Fathers, and at the same time that this did not interfere with their view of the prerogatives of St. Peter."},{"id":"60e4e294f2da","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":38,"p":[17,17],"r":[12,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zechariah chapter 12, verse 10"},{"id":"f22cbdb87179","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":23,"p":[34,34],"r":[1,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zechariah chapter 1, verse 15"},{"id":"531aa4a0b1c6","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1tim","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1tim","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":1,"p":[1,1],"r":[13,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xiii. 7"},{"id":"979f05b5d831","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":102,"p":[1,1],"r":[2,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"cf . Zech. ii. 8.","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"7a6aaa627741","v":"npnf.basilius.epistulae","w":"basilius.epistulae","a":"basilius_von_casarea","s":210,"p":[6,6],"r":[10,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. x. 1, 2,"},{"id":"9622dc3b7114","v":"npnf.gregor_nyssa.contra_eunomi