gregor_von_nazianz","s":2,"p":[118,118],"r":[11,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xi. 15."},{"id":"313303651180","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":9,"p":[19,19],"r":[11,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xi. 5."},{"id":"912dece06f4f","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":9,"p":[20,20],"r":[5,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. v. 8."},{"id":"b8b180320cac","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":9,"p":[21,21],"r":[11,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xi. 2."},{"id":"1873f0c7deba","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":15,"p":[2,2],"r":[11,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Prov. viii. 22. The A.V. has in the place Possessed, and this has very high authority: but the Hebrew word in almost every case signifies to Acquire. It is used, says Bp. Wordsworth (ad h. l.), about eighty times in the O. T., and in only five places is it rendered in our Translation by Possess; - in two of which (Gen. xiv. 10, 22, and Ps. cxxxix. 13) it might well have the sense of Creating, and in two (Jer. xxxii. 15, and Zech. xi. 5) of Getting. In some ancient Versions (LXX. and Syr.) it is rendered by Create. S. Jerome in his Ep. and Cypr. (ii. 697) says that the word may here be understood of possession, but in his Comm. on Ephes. ii. (p. 342) he adopts the rendering Create, which he applies to the Incarnation, as in several places does S. Athanasius. But Wordsworth thinks it better to apply the words to the Eternal Generation, as S. Hilary expounds it (c. Arianos, who argued from it that Christ was a creature): \"quia Filius Dei non corporalis parturitionis est genitus exemplo, sed ex perfecto Deo perfectus Deus natus; et ideo ait creatam se esse Sapientia; omnem in generatione sua notionem passionis corporalis excludens.\""},{"id":"01ed04dcc5db","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":15,"p":[2,2],"r":[13,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xiii. 7."},{"id":"583869d236ca","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":21,"p":[24,24],"r":[4,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. iv. 7."},{"id":"84a671322318","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":23,"p":[9,9],"r":[3,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. iii. 9 ."},{"id":"42e5a39fa3ac","v":"npnf.gregor_naz.orationes","w":"gregor_naz.orationes","a":"gregor_von_nazianz","s":24,"p":[7,7],"r":[11,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xi. 2."},{"id":"fb26a7b0396b","v":"npnf.ephraem.hymni_de_nativitate","w":"ephraem.hymni_de_nativitate","a":"ephram_der_syrer","s":2,"p":[8,8],"r":[3,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. iii. 3."},{"id":"09fcd21abf22","v":"npnf.ephraem.de_margarita","w":"ephraem.de_margarita","a":"ephram_der_syrer","s":1,"p":[42,42],"r":[2,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Zech. ii. 8.","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"f251b797da7d","v":"npnf.theodoret.eranistes","w":"theodoret.eranistes","a":"theodoret_von_cyrus","s":2,"p":[479,479],"r":[12,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xii. 10."},{"id":"8841ec64d140","v":"npnf.theodoret.eranistes","w":"theodoret.eranistes","a":"theodoret_von_cyrus","s":2,"p":[598,598],"r":[12,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zechariah xii. 10."},{"id":"31fe68dd6d4a","v":"npnf.theodoret.historia_ecclesiastica","w":"theodoret.historia_ecclesiastica","a":"theodoret_von_cyrus","s":1,"p":[120,120],"r":[14,20],"k":"