sus_marcionem","w":"tertullian.adversus_marcionem","a":"tertullian","s":4,"p":[84,84],"r":[14,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. xiv. 4."},{"id":"a2916c98a035","v":"anf.tertullian.adversus_marcionem","w":"tertullian.adversus_marcionem","a":"tertullian","s":4,"p":[86,86],"r":[11,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"This passage more nearly resembles Zech. xi. 12 and 13 than anything in Jeremiah, although the transaction in Jer. xxxii. 7-15 is noted by the commentators, as referred to. Tertullian had good reason for mentioning Jeremiah and not Zechariah, because the apostle whom he refers to (Matt. xxvii. 3-10) had distinctly attributed the prophecy to Jeremiah (\"Jeremy the prophet,\" ver. 9). This is not the plcae to do more than emrely refer to the voluminous controversy which has arisen from the apostle's mention of Jeremiah instead of Zechariah. It is enough to remark that Tertullian's argument is unaffected by the discrepancy in the name of the particular prophet. On all hands the prophecy is admitted, and this at once satisifes our author's argument. For the ms. evidence in favour of the unquestionably correct reading, τότε ἐπληρώθη τὸ ῥηθὲν διὰ 9Ieremi/ou τοὺ προφήτου, k.t.l. , the reader is referred to Dr. Tregelles' Critical Greek Testament, in loc. ; only to the convincing amount of evidence collected by the very leraned editor must now be added the subsequently obtained authority of Tischendorf's Codex Sinaiticus ."},{"id":"aa063dc6c7a9","v":"anf.origenes.contra_celsum","w":"origenes.contra_celsum","a":"origenes","s":6,"p":[51,51],"r":[5,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Cf. Zech. v. 7"},{"id":"ac78b223cf4a","v":"anf.origenes.de_principiis","w":"origenes.de_principiis","a":"origenes","s":5,"p":[51,51],"r":[3,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. iii. 1."},{"id":"d67eb81a30f4","v":"anf.origenes.de_principiis","w":"origenes.de_principiis","a":"origenes","s":5,"p":[55,55],"r":[1,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Zech. i. 14. The Vulgate, Septuagint, and Masoretic text all have \"in me,\" although the Authorized Version reads \"with me.\""},{"id":"61c2c65c7338","v":"csel.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":35,"p":[0,0],"r":[13,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Zach. 13, 2; Esai. 19, 1; Lc. 2, 25; Matth. 16, 16; Ephes. 4, 14","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"},{"id":"3b56a554ab01","v":"csel.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":90,"p":[3,3],"r":[9,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Agg. 2, 7; Zach. 9, 9","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"},{"id":"c16f8cd94135","v":"csel.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":90,"p":[3,3],"r":[9,11],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Zach. 9, 11; Ps. 39, 3; Mal. 1, 10","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"},{"id":"22a73cf82732","v":"csel.augustinus.de_civitate_dei","w":"augustinus.de_civitate_dei","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":110,"p":[0,0],"r":[12,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Mt. 15, 24; Io. 7, 39; Ps. 17, 44; Lc. 5, 10; Zach. 12, 9","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"},{"id":"a8a1a55d8b33","v":"csel.augustinus.de_peccatorum_meritis","w":"augustinus.de_peccatorum_meritis","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":7,"p":[4,4],"r":[1,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"II Cor. 5, 4; Matth. 6,13; Rom. 8, 5; Zach. 1,3; Mal.3,5; Ps. 79,8","note":"Stellenangabe im Apparat der Ausgabe (Seite; Absatz ungefähr)"},{"id":"a0ff508d032a","v":"csel.augustinus.de_nuptiis","w":"augustinus.de_nuptiis","a":"augustinus_von_hippo","s":10,"p"